exercises.explanation:
Override only `toString`; the generated `equals` and `hashCode` stay:

```java
record Credentials(String user, String password) {
    @Override public String toString() { return "Credentials[user=" + user + ", password=***]"; }
}
```

The tests catch the plausible wrong masks. Masking only when the password is non-empty (`password.isEmpty() ? "" : "***"`) tells a reader which accounts have no password and throws on `null` (the boundary test). Clearing the password in the compact constructor instead of masking the output does hide it, but two different passwords then compare equal (the equals test). Overriding `user()` or `password()` accessors has no effect on `toString`, which reads the fields.
